message: "If you use SysSimX in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SysSimX: A Python Framework for Heterogeneous Hybrid Co-Simulation"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Florian
    family-names: Frech
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add your ORCID before the release
    # email:           # optional
version: 0.1.7
date-released: 2026-06-11   # set to the actual submission/release date
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/FlorianFrech/SystemSimulation"
url: "https://syssimx.readthedocs.io/"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"   # uncomment after Zenodo mints the version DOI
abstract: >-
  SysSimX is a Python framework for heterogeneous hybrid co-simulation
  with runtime model switching. It couples Functional Mock-up Units
  (FMUs), OpenSim models, and finite-element method (FEM) models through
  a shared component abstraction, derives structural execution metadata
  for initialization, master algorithm execution, and algebraic-loop
  handling, and supports hybrid event localization and runtime switching
  between alternative models of the same subsystem.
keywords:
  - co-simulation
  - hybrid systems
  - heterogeneous simulation
  - runtime model switching
  - FMI
  - OpenSim
  - finite-element method
  - Python
